{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLyWTWA97JH4Rj8j9PFm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast runs checkout` and `npx roast runs prune` are implemented, and every checklist item in ticket 24 is done. The final gate passed: `npm test` ran 7127 of 7127 tests, lint and typecheck are clean, and `go build ./...` and `npm run test:go` both exit 0. All work is in 8 commits on the branch. The notes file in `.redeye/notes.md` is not committed, as instructed.\n\n**What was added**\n- **`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts`:** `load`, `restore`, `removeWorktree`, `prune` and `Pruned`. `restore` and `removeWorktree` remove `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from the environment for every git call they make. A restore that fails after `worktree add` removes the half-built worktree before rethrowing.\n- **`src/cli/runs.ts`:**\n  - **`checkout <run-id> [dir]`:** finds the run by unique ID prefix and restores from the repository path recorded in `meta.json`. A relative `dir` is resolved once against the command's working directory. Stdout is only the destination path.\n  - **`prune`:** supports `--older-than` (default `720h`) and `--dry-run`, and prints `deleted` / `would delete` lines with the age rounded to the hour.\n  - **Exit codes:** usage errors exit 2; restore and prune failures exit 4.\n- **Tests:** `test/snapshot/restore.ts` covers the module, and `test/cli/runs-snapshot.ts` covers the CLI after a real review against the fake server. Some tests passed as soon as they were written, so I checked them by breaking the code on purpose. Removing the `GIT_INDEX_FILE` clearing, the failed-restore cleanup, the working-directory resolution, the \"snapshot captured\" check, or the usage-error wrapping each makes a test fail.\n\n**Choices that differ from the spec's wording**\n- **`prune` arguments:** it takes `now` inside an options object rather than as a fourth argument. That matches how the rest of the snapshot module passes `env` and `signal`.\n- **Fractional threshold:** `prune` accepts the threshold as fractional milliseconds. Otherwise `--older-than 1ns` would round down to 0 and fall back to 30 days, which would break the ticket's own test case.\n\n**Gaps**\n- Nothing tests the default destination used when `dir` is omitted (`roast-checkout-` under the temp directory), because no checklist item asks for it.\n- That default uses `os.tmpdir()`, which reads the process's `TMPDIR` rather than the environment passed to the command.\n- The exact format of the age text in prune output is not asserted, since it is human-readable output.\n\nI added notes for future snapshot work to `docs/agents/scope-context.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":136565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":766,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de572ae-0eae-4979-b0e7-cefd41e0bbfc","uuid":"b6636a66-0206-499b-9f99-63b6a8bad7ec","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:36:48.100Z","request_id":"req_011ChLyWTLjvWgaVr6pULczy"}
